# Every path the format row skips. The row passes --ignore-path .prettierignore,
# so .gitignore narrows nothing, and CODEOWNERS routes every change here to the
# code owner's review. A leading slash anchors an entry to the root, so a file
# of that name below it is still checked.

# Written by release-please on every release. Its bullets are asterisks and its
# version headers carry a blank line prettier would collapse, so formatting it
# turns each release into a failing check on main. The manifest is written on
# one line by the same tool.
/CHANGELOG.md
/.release-please-manifest.json
# Written by cmd/generate, whose table is not column-aligned the way prettier
# wants it. The generate task checks it by regenerating, not by formatting.
/MARKERS.md

# Local-only paths .gitignore names that can hold a file Prettier reads: build
# and coverage output, editor settings, local notes, lefthook's per-user
# overrides, and Claude Code's per-machine settings, reviews and worktrees.
/dist/
/coverage.*
/.idea/
/.vscode/
/*.local.*
/lefthook-local.*
/.lefthook-local.*
/.lefthook-local/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/review/
.claude/worktrees/
